---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
---

<Section
  id="lanes"
  title="A second worktree comes up next to main, on its own ports."
  more={{ href: '/lanes/', label: 'More about lanes' }}
>
  <p>
    Each lane gets a block of ports and its own hostnames, such as <code>myapp1.localhost</code>.
    Run the checkout branch alongside main without assigning ports in <code>.env</code> files or
    editing a proxy by hand.
  </p>
  <p>
    Heavy infra such as a database server runs once and is shared, with a database per lane inside
    it, so a migration in one lane leaves main's data alone. Lanes that need their own containers
    get them. One committed <code>devlanes.yaml</code> describes the stack for every lane.
  </p>
  <Terminal slot="visual" title="~/dev/myapp-checkout">
    <pre class="terminal-content"><span class="command">$ git worktree add ../myapp-checkout -b feat/checkout</span>
<span class="dim">Preparing worktree (new branch 'feat/checkout')</span>
<span class="command">$ cd ../myapp-checkout</span>
<span class="command">$ devlanes start --no-ui</span>
myapp@1 · feat/checkout
<span class="success">✓</span> services  3 of 3 ready
  <span class="success">✓</span>  api     <span class="url">https://api.myapp1.localhost</span>
  <span class="success">✓</span>  web     <span class="url">https://myapp1.localhost</span>
  <span class="success">✓</span>  worker  http://127.0.0.1:20012</pre>
  </Terminal>
</Section>
